### Example 3: Timer0 Delay (Polling)
This example uses Timer0 to create a delay without using the blocking `_delay_ms()` function. It toggles an LED on PORT C.0.

```c
/*
 * Target: ATmega32
 * Description: Blinks an LED using Timer0 in normal mode.
 * Instead of using _delay_ms(), we poll the Timer Overflow Flag (TOV0).
 * With an 8MHz clock and no prescaler, Timer0 overflows every 256us.
 * To get ~500ms, we count ~1953 overflows (0.5s / 0.000256s).
 */
#include <avr/io.h>

int main(void) {
    DDRC |= (1 << PC0); // Set PC0 as output for LED

    // Timer0 Control Register:
    // CS00 = 1 means no prescaling (Timer ticks at system clock speed)
    TCCR0 = (1 << CS00); 

    // Variable to count the number of overflows
    unsigned int overflow_count = 0;

    while (1) {
        // Wait until Timer0 overflows (TOV0 flag becomes 1)
        while (!(TIFR & (1 << TOV0)));

        // Clear the TOV0 flag by writing a logical 1 to it
        TIFR = (1 << TOV0);

        overflow_count++;

        // 1953 overflows * 256us = ~500ms
        if (overflow_count >= 1953) {
            // Toggle the LED on PC0
            PORTC ^= (1 << PC0);

            // Reset the overflow counter
            overflow_count = 0;
        }
    }
}
```

